# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("The label that lags") as moved by rulings ST and VL (round 3): the `rebuild`'s result is structural and changes the tick after its generation is built, and `@Flatten` adopts at the end of that tick, so the label follows two owed ticks after the click (as sem-ch08-viewer).
test the_label_lags

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="next")
    1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")
    2: Ui.Label(text="showing 1")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    1/#1/0: Ui.Label(text="page 2")
  torn down:
    1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")

tick 2

tick 3
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="showing 2")
